CHAPTER.VERS:
This is now, beloved, the second letter that I write to you

          {+}
        ; and in both of them I stir up your

          {+}
         sincere mind by putting you

          {+}
         in remembrance;

that you

          {+}
         should remember the words which were spoken before by the holy prophets, and the commandments of the Lord and Savior through your

          {+}
         apostles:

The Lord is not slack concerning his promise, as some count slackness; but is long-suffering toward you

          {+}
        , not wishing that any should perish, but that all should come to repentance.

Seeing that these things are thus all to be dissolved, what manner of persons ought you

          {+}
         to be in [all] holy living and godliness,

Therefore, beloved, seeing that you

          {+}
         look for these things, be diligent that you

          {+}
         may be found in peace, without spot and blameless in his sight.

And account that the long-suffering of our Lord is salvation; even as our beloved brother Paul also, according to the wisdom given to him, wrote to you

          {+}
        ;

You

          {+}
         therefore, beloved, knowing [these things] beforehand, beware lest, being carried away with the error of the wicked, you

          {+}
         fall from your

          {+}
         own steadfastness.
